Go.dot patch 0003 for Tracktion Engine: AudioClipPlayhead's state initialised.

Clang with GCC 15's libstdc++ (Ubuntu 26.04, or the NUC with g++-15) does not
compile Tracktion: libstdc++ 15 constrains std::atomic<T>'s default constructor
on T being default-constructible, and AudioClipPlayhead::State - a nested class
with default member initialisers - is not, to Clang, until AudioClipPlayhead is
complete; make_shared<AudioClipPlayhead>() in AudioClipBase then has no
constructor to call. GCC itself and libc++ (macOS) accept it. Initialising the
member asks for State's constructor, not atomic's, and changes nothing else.
Upstreamable as it stands; drop it when Tracktion carries the same. The line
carries a notice that Go.dot modified it (GPL-3, section 5(a)).

Applied by Go.dot's build, cmake/WfgSubmodulePatches.cmake, in the order
patches/tracktion_engine/series gives; refreshed from the working tree with
scripts/patches.py tracktion_engine refresh, which keeps this header. Against
Tracktion Engine a5e44996f5f0.

diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h
index 45733adbab4..e4230323776 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/model/clips/tracktion_AudioClipBase.h
@@ -52,7 +52,11 @@ private:
         uint32_t lastUpdateMs = 0;
     };
 
-    std::atomic<State> state;
+    // Go.dot modified this line, 2026-11-19, patch 0003-clang-libstdcxx15-playhead:
+    // initialised, so std::atomic's default constructor (constrained on State
+    // being default-constructible, which a nested class with member
+    // initialisers is not until the enclosing class is complete) is not needed.
+    std::atomic<State> state { State {} };
 };
 
